main: cannot import "example.com/util": no pluto.mod declares a module, so only pluto/ packages can be imported
    Without a pluto.mod file, a program is a single package that can import only
    the standard library (paths under pluto/). To split a program into packages,
    add a pluto.mod file in its top directory that names the module, and import
    packages by the module path followed by their directory.
    Create pluto.mod in the top directory:
        module example.com/project

        // and import a package in ./util as:
        import "example.com/project/util"
    (run "pluto explain E4007" for a longer explanation)
